{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 40","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For what value(s) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> will this system have infinitely many solutions?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1e870007193d97df507d7ed44d205ede277eb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 3x+2y&amp;=8\\\\ 6x+ky&amp;=16 \\end{align*}\" width=\"102\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed1be907dce28186c12053c188068c35240c7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  k=-2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  k=0 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  k=4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  k=6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  \\text{All real numbers} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"647\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the system of equations to have infinitely many solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942e8bf1bae65e931952a73a0fc771c86b0ff059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{3} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> times the original coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e3cd3ca4a8e4d98712fc963a96d6d68c9b79a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2 \\times 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"156\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>¬anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 39\">Problem 39</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wik